  "summary": "A glamorous interwar style of stepped forms, symmetry, chrome and exotic material pairings celebrating the machine age.",
  "description": "Named after the 1925 Paris Exposition Internationale des Arts Décoratifs, Art Deco fused Cubist geometry, Ballets Russes color, Egyptian and Aztec motifs and machine aesthetics into skyscrapers, ocean liners, cinemas and radios. Zigzag Moderne gave way to Streamline Moderne's rounded aerodynamics. From Manhattan to Shanghai to Mumbai, it signalled modern luxury. Its symmetrical marquetry and stepped ziggurat silhouettes keep returning in revival design.",
